### Access API flow (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client)
#
# Prereq: server running (`npm run start:dev`) and one api-key doc in Mongo, e.g.
#   db['api-keys'].insertOne({ key: 'dev-key-0000', status: true, permissions: ['0000'] })
# Every request passes checkAuth (x-api-key) then permission('0000').

@host = http://localhost:5005
@apiKey = dev-key-0000
@email = shop-{{$timestamp}}@example.com

### 1. Health check, valid key -> 200 Hello world
GET {{host}}/
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

### 2. No x-api-key header -> 403 Forbidden error
GET {{host}}/

### 3. Unknown x-api-key -> 403 Forbidden error
GET {{host}}/
x-api-key: not-a-real-key

### 4. Sign up a new shop -> 201, metadata.shop + metadata.tokens
POST {{host}}/api/v1/shop/signup
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "name": "Shop Test",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "123456"
}

### 5. Sign up without api key -> 403 Forbidden error
POST {{host}}/api/v1/shop/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Shop Test",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "123456"
}

### 6. Sign up again with same email (run 4 first, reuse its email) -> expect an error, see note
# NOTE: {{email}} is regenerated per request, so paste the email from request 4 here.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/shop/signup
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "name": "Shop Test",
  "email": "PASTE-EMAIL-FROM-REQUEST-4",
  "password": "123456"
}
